<%# The board at one moment of a game, with nothing to click.

    The replay page draws itself from this: it is handed a Draughts::Position parsed straight
    out of a stored 32-character string and the two squares of the move that led to it. Every
    square goes through the same matches/square partial the playable board uses, with playable
    false, which renders each one as a disabled button carrying its accessible label. So a
    replayed board looks and reads exactly like a live one, keeps the tint on the last move's
    origin and destination (rubric 39), and cannot be used to play: there is no form on this
    page and no square is a control.

    The id is replay-board, not the live board's, because nothing replaces this fragment: the
    replay subscribes to nothing and broadcasts nothing. %>
<div id="replay-board" class="board-zone">
  <div class="board" role="group" aria-label="<%= label %>">
    <% board_cells.each do |number| %>
      <% if number.nil? %>
        <div class="board__cell board__cell--light" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <% else %>
        <%= render "matches/square", match: match, number: number, piece: position.at(number),
              selection: nil, target: false,
              last_move_end: last_move_end(number, tinted.first, tinted.last),
              playable: false, pending: false, own_targets: nil %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
